From b59f6ae6f95f66a90dde65ecfbe0f535e029bbfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:09:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dwc2d: card readers (one disk per LUN with a card) and
 several sticks at once

A card reader has one logical unit per slot. GET MAX LUN gives their
number, and every command carries its LUN; each LUN with a medium is a
disk of the reader's scheme under its number
(disk.usb-dwc2+<ports>-scsi/<lun>, so a stick stays .../0). An empty
slot answers "medium not present" and is left out at once instead of
after 5 s of waiting.

Sticks and readers no longer come one at a time: each gets its own
scheme, all share host channels 4 and 5 (one command at a time). The
log names the scheme when a device is removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
